sentence(s_book_01_0095, 'book', 1, 85, 'unmarked', "Modern Alchemy, the companion reference, holds these concepts as a numbered glossary with a notation for combining them.").
sentence(s_book_01_0096, 'book', 1, 85, 'unmarked', "It is more useful alongside the book than before it.").
sentence(s_book_01_0097, 'book', 1, 87, 'unmarked', "A note on what the book is for.").
sentence(s_book_01_0098, 'book', 1, 87, 'unmarked', "It is not an argument that is supposed to end in agreement.").
sentence(s_book_01_0099, 'book', 1, 87, 'unmarked', "It is an attempt to make a set of transitions describable — from chemistry that persists, to chemistry that copies, to systems that model, to systems that tell each other what they have modelled — using terms that travel between them without pretending the territory is the same.").
sentence(s_book_01_0100, 'book', 1, 87, 'unmarked', "Where the terms travel well, something has been gained.").
sentence(s_book_01_0101, 'book', 1, 87, 'unmarked', "Where they travel badly, that is worth knowing too, and the book tries to be useful about both.").
chapter('book', 2, "02-vocabulary-of-emergence.md", "2. A recurring vocabulary of emergence").
sentence(s_book_02_0001, 'book', 2, 3, 'unmarked', "A small number of concepts recur across every domain this book covers.").
sentence(s_book_02_0002, 'book', 2, 3, 'unmarked', "They are set out here so that later chapters can use them without redefining them, and so that the reader can hold the whole set in view at once.").
sentence(s_book_02_0003, 'book', 2, 5, 'unmarked', "A warning belongs before the list rather than after it.").
sentence(s_book_02_0004, 'book', 2, 5, 'unmarked', "These terms travel well, and that is exactly what makes them dangerous.").
sentence(s_book_02_0005, 'book', 2, 5, 'unmarked', "A word that correctly applies to a chemical reaction and to a language has not shown that the two have anything in common beyond being describable.").
number(s_book_02_0005, 2, 'have').
keywords(s_book_02_0005, ['anything', 'apply', 'beyond', 'chemical', 'common', 'correctly', 'describable', 'language', 'reaction', 'shown']).
sentence(s_book_02_0006, 'book', 2, 5, 'unmarked', "A later section of this chapter takes that seriously enough to work through an example.").
sentence(s_book_02_0007, 'book', 2, 9, 'unmarked', "The production of differences within a system.").
sentence(s_book_02_0008, 'book', 2, 9, 'unmarked', "Variation arises through random events, environmental fluctuation, recombination, mutation, experimentation, or deliberate action.").
sentence(s_book_02_0009, 'book', 2, 11, 'unmarked', "The exploration of possible states or combinations.").
sentence(s_book_02_0010, 'book', 2, 11, 'unmarked', "Search requires no intention, no intelligence, and no objective.").
sentence(s_book_02_0011, 'book', 2, 11, 'unmarked', "A mixture of molecules bumping into one another is searching, in the only sense this book needs.").
sentence(s_book_02_0012, 'book', 2, 13, 'unmarked', "The differential persistence or success of some configurations over others.").
sentence(s_book_02_0013, 'book', 2, 13, 'unmarked', "Selection can be imposed by environmental conditions, physical stability, resource availability, competition, compatibility, or any other constraint that treats configurations unequally.").
sentence(s_book_02_0014, 'book', 2, 15, 'unmarked', "The persistence of a configuration over time — through chemical stability, feedback, replication, memory, physical structure, or institutional practice.").
sentence(s_book_02_0015, 'book', 2, 17, 'unmarked', "A process by which an existing pattern or difference becomes more abundant or more influential.").
sentence(s_book_02_0016, 'book', 2, 17, 'unmarked', "Positive feedback amplifies small initial differences, sometimes enormously.").
sentence(s_book_02_0017, 'book', 2, 19, 'unmarked', "The local accumulation of matter, energy, or information.").
sentence(s_book_02_0018, 'book', 2, 19, 'unmarked', "Processes that are negligible at low density can dominate at high density, so concentration frequently decides what is possible.").
sentence(s_book_02_0019, 'book', 2, 21, 'unmarked', "The formation of a boundary that localizes processes and permits conditions inside to differ from conditions outside.").
sentence(s_book_02_0020, 'book', 2, 21, 'unmarked', "Chapter 5 is about why this changes so much.").
xref(s_book_02_0020, 5).
sentence(s_book_02_0021, 'book', 2, 23, 'unmarked', "Compartments nested within, or integrated into, larger compartments.").
sentence(s_book_02_0022, 'book', 2, 25, 'unmarked', "The linking of processes so that one supports, regulates, or enables another.").
sentence(s_book_02_0023, 'book', 2, 25, 'unmarked', "Coupling is how separate things become one system.").
sentence(s_book_02_0024, 'book', 2, 27, 'unmarked', "The development of components that perform particular functions.").
sentence(s_book_02_0025, 'book', 2, 27, 'unmarked', "It improves what the whole can do and costs each part its independence.").
sentence(s_book_02_0026, 'book', 2, 29, 'unmarked', "The reduction of complex information into more manageable representations.").
sentence(s_book_02_0027, 'book', 2, 29, 'unmarked', "Compression makes information easier to store, process, and transmit, and necessarily discards something.").
sentence(s_book_02_0028, 'book', 2, 31, 'unmarked', "The movement of information, structure, or behaviour between components, organisms, generations, or populations.").
sentence(s_book_02_0029, 'book', 2, 33, 'unmarked', "The retention and layering of change over time.").
sentence(s_book_02_0030, 'book', 2, 33, 'unmarked', "Accumulation is what makes a history rather than a sequence of unrelated states.").
sentence(s_book_02_0031, 'book', 2, 35, 'unmarked', "A process in which a system's output influences its subsequent behaviour.").
sentence(s_book_02_0032, 'book', 2, 35, 'unmarked', "Feedback stabilizes, amplifies, regulates, or destabilizes, depending on its sign and strength.").
sentence(s_book_02_0033, 'book', 2, 37, 'unmarked', "The appearance of system-level properties arising from interactions among components — properties not apparent from examining any component alone.").
sentence(s_book_02_0034, 'book', 2, 39, 'unmarked', "Observing what persisted rather than everything that was tried.").
sentence(s_book_02_0035, 'book', 2, 39, 'unmarked', "This belongs in the list because it is a property of the observer rather than of the system, and because it distorts every question in this book.").
sentence(s_book_02_0036, 'book', 2, 39, 'unmarked', "Chapter 3 shows how severely.").
xref(s_book_02_0036, 3).
sentence(s_book_02_0037, 'book', 2, 43, 'unmarked', "These are descriptive terms, not explanatory ones.").
sentence(s_book_02_0038, 'book', 2, 43, 'unmarked', "Saying that a system underwent variation and selection says what happened at a level of abstraction that deliberately omits the machinery.").
sentence(s_book_02_0039, 'book', 2, 43, 'unmarked', "That abstraction is useful for noticing that two situations rhyme.").
number(s_book_02_0039, 2, 'situation').
keywords(s_book_02_0039, ['abstraction', 'noticing', 'rhyme', 'situation', 'useful']).
sentence(s_book_02_0040, 'book', 2, 43, 'unmarked', "It is useless for establishing that they work alike, and the step from one to the other is where arguments of this kind usually fail.").
sentence(s_book_02_0041, 'book', 2, 45, 'unmarked', "The terms are also not independent.").
sentence(s_book_02_0042, 'book', 2, 45, 'unmarked', "Compression tends to follow specialization, because a specialized component does not need the information a general one does.").
sentence(s_book_02_0043, 'book', 2, 45, 'unmarked', "Amplification requires feedback.").
sentence(s_book_02_0044, 'book', 2, 45, 'unmarked', "Accumulation requires retention.").
sentence(s_book_02_0045, 'book', 2, 45, 'unmarked', "The vocabulary describes a connected set of processes rather than a checklist.").
sentence(s_book_02_0046, 'book', 2, 49, 'unmarked', "The clearest way to hold the warning is to take one term and watch it change underneath.").
sentence(s_book_02_0047, 'book', 2, 57, 'unmarked', "Three rows under the heading \"selection.").
number(s_book_02_0047, 3, 'row').
keywords(s_book_02_0047, ['heading', 'selection', 'three']).
sentence(s_book_02_0048, 'book', 2, 57, 'unmarked', "The processes share no machinery.").
sentence(s_book_02_0049, 'book', 2, 57, 'unmarked', "Chemical persistence involves no population and no copying.").
sentence(s_book_02_0050, 'book', 2, 57, 'unmarked', "Biological selection requires a replicating template and operates across generations.").
sentence(s_book_02_0051, 'book', 2, 57, 'unmarked', "Cultural selection operates within a single lifetime, passes between unrelated people, runs in any direction including backwards in age, and copies with such low fidelity that the thing transmitted is frequently not the thing that was sent.").
sentence(s_book_02_0052, 'book', 2, 59, 'unmarked', "Any sentence applying \"selection\" across these rows is doing less work than it appears to.").
hedged(s_book_02_0052).
sentence(s_book_02_0053, 'book', 2, 59, 'unmarked', "What the shared term buys is the question — is something being varied, and is something treating the variants unequally? — which is worth asking in all three cases.").
number(s_book_02_0053, 3, 'case').
keywords(s_book_02_0053, ['asking', 'question', 'shared', 'something', 'three', 'treating', 'unequally', 'variant', 'varied', 'worth']).
sentence(s_book_02_0054, 'book', 2, 59, 'unmarked', "The answer is different every time, and the answer is the part that matters.").
sentence(s_book_02_0055, 'book', 2, 63, 'unmarked', "These concepts and roughly a hundred more are set out in Modern Alchemy, the companion volume, with permanent identifiers, one symbol each, and a notation for combining them.").
number(s_book_02_0055, 100, 'set').
keywords(s_book_02_0055, ['alchemy', 'combining', 'companion', 'concept', 'hundred', 'identifier', 'modern', 'notation', 'permanent', 'symbol', 'volume']).
sentence(s_book_02_0056, 'book', 2, 63, 'unmarked', "It is deliberately oversimplified and says so on its first page.").
sentence(s_book_02_0057, 'book', 2, 65, 'unmarked', "The notation exists to make combining easy.").
sentence(s_book_02_0058, 'book', 2, 65, 'unmarked', "A field cannot be held in the head, but a handle can, and handles can be set side by side.").
certainty_word(s_book_02_0058, 'cannot be').
sentence(s_book_02_0059, 'book', 2, 65, 'unmarked', "Each concept gets a symbol, and a few operators join them: + for things acting together, → for \"can produce, under conditions not stated,\" ≈ for a resemblance that claims no shared mechanism.").
sentence(s_book_02_0060, 'book', 2, 65, 'unmarked', "An argument that takes pages in chapter 5 then fits on a line — Ap + Df → V, amphiphiles diffusing in water can close into a vesicle — and that line can be laid beside a line from another field to see whether they rhyme.").
xref(s_book_02_0060, 5).
sentence(s_book_02_0061, 'book', 2, 65, 'unmarked', "Most cross-domain questions begin as exactly that kind of naive juxtaposition.").
sentence(s_book_02_0062, 'book', 2, 65, 'unmarked', "The book's whole arc, from thermodynamics to the evolution of religion, fits in a few lines of it.").
sentence(s_book_02_0063, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "The name is a joke with a point in it.").
sentence(s_book_02_0064, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "Alchemy had a working notation, real apparatus, and a conviction that the right combinations would reveal how matter worked.").
sentence(s_book_02_0065, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "It was wrong about nearly everything, and chemistry grew out of it anyway.").
sentence(s_book_02_0066, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "Its symbols also combined as smoothly for a transmutation that never worked as for a distillation that did, and the same holds here: symbols always compose, and the world is under no obligation to follow.").
certainty_word(s_book_02_0066, 'never').
certainty_word(s_book_02_0066, 'always').
sentence(s_book_02_0067, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "So a formula is a question rather than a finding.").
sentence(s_book_02_0068, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "Analogies are written with ≈ and kept away from the arrow on purpose, because an analogy taken for a mechanism is the error this book most needs to avoid.").
sentence(s_book_02_0069, 'book', 2, 67, 'unmarked', "And a formula is silent on rates, probabilities, scale, and reversibility, and records only what persisted.").
sentence(s_book_02_0070, 'book', 2, 69, 'unmarked', "It is most useful alongside this book rather than before it, and its closing sections, on what the notation cannot express and on using it without being fooled, make the same point this chapter has just made, at greater length and with less patience.").
sentence(s_book_02_0071, 'book', 2, 69, 'unmarked', "The fact checker described in chapter 1 reads its worked chains as well, and tests that every step of the arc either has a chain behind it or is named as a gap.").
