sentence(s_bookhs_16_0032, 'book-hs', 16, 27, 'unmarked', "Here is the serious objection to this book, put as well as I can put it:").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0033, 'book-hs', 16, 29, 'unmarked', "It's an interesting story and too broad to count as a real theory.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0034, 'book-hs', 16, 29, 'unmarked', "It links a lot of fields by analogy without isolating sharp, testable mechanisms that would let it be decisively right or wrong.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0035, 'book-hs', 16, 29, 'unmarked', "It risks explaining too much with one pattern.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0036, 'book-hs', 16, 29, 'unmarked', "And it doesn't predict anything that ordinary science in those fields wouldn't predict anyway.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0037, 'book-hs', 16, 31, 'unmarked', "Every clause of that is fair.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0038, 'book-hs', 16, 33, 'unmarked', "The worst one is \"explains too much.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0039, 'book-hs', 16, 33, 'unmarked', "A pattern you can find everywhere constrains nothing.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0040, 'book-hs', 16, 33, 'unmarked', "A framework that no observation could embarrass isn't telling you anything.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0041, 'book-hs', 16, 35, 'unmarked', "And it gets worse.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0042, 'book-hs', 16, 35, 'unmarked', "The ability to find patterns everywhere is exactly the unreliable faculty from chapter 13 — and exactly what the opening of this book describes me doing at unusual intensity.").
