sentence(s_bookhs_16_0088, 'book-hs', 16, 73, 'unmarked', "Fair question, and the answer is thinner than I'd like.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0089, 'book-hs', 16, 75, 'unmarked', "The cheapest test is one nobody has run, including me.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0090, 'book-hs', 16, 75, 'unmarked', "Generate systems with no real structure in them, describe them in this book's vocabulary, and see whether anyone can tell them from the real ones.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0091, 'book-hs', 16, 75, 'unmarked', "If the words fit random junk just as well, then this book describes the describer and not the world.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0092, 'book-hs', 16, 77, 'unmarked', "Beyond that: if someone found a single mechanism that genuinely did unify all these fields, the book's central hedge would be wrong in the opposite direction.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0093, 'book-hs', 16, 77, 'unmarked', "And if the origin of copying gets explained by chemistry that owes nothing to variation, selection, or compression, then this vocabulary was decoration over the interesting part.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0094, 'book-hs', 16, 79, 'unmarked', "That last one is the most likely of the three.").
