sentence(s_bookhs_16_0098, 'book-hs', 16, 85, 'unmarked', "\"We don't know what this is for\" and \"this has no purpose\" are different claims, and the first keeps getting mistaken for the second.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0099, 'book-hs', 16, 85, 'unmarked', "That's a good habit to carry out of this book and into everything else.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0100, 'book-hs', 16, 89, 'unmarked', "The point of the vocabulary is to make a set of changes easier to see and talk about, without pretending they work the same way.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0101, 'book-hs', 16, 89, 'unmarked', "That's a modest aim and it's the one the evidence supports.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0102, 'book-hs', 16, 91, 'unmarked', "You can finish this book believing very different things about what it adds up to.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0103, 'book-hs', 16, 91, 'unmarked', "Nothing here is built to move you.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0104, 'book-hs', 16, 91, 'unmarked', "It doesn't settle whether there's a purpose behind any of it, whether the patterns point at anything, or what to make of the fact that some matter on one planet ended up able to ask.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0105, 'book-hs', 16, 93, 'unmarked', "What it offers is an account where the steps connect.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0106, 'book-hs', 16, 93, 'unmarked', "Chemistry that lasts, boundaries that hold, networks that feed themselves, patterns that copy, systems that model, minds that tell each other what they modelled.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0107, 'book-hs', 16, 95, 'unmarked', "One word there needs care.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0108, 'book-hs', 16, 95, 'unmarked', "There is a break in this account, at copying, and it's not small.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0109, 'book-hs', 16, 97, 'unmarked', "But there are two meanings of \"break\" and they have to be kept apart.").
number(s_bookhs_16_0109, 2, 'meaning').
keywords(s_bookhs_16_0109, ['apart', 'break', 'meaning']).
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0110, 'book-hs', 16, 97, 'unmarked', "A break in the account is a hole in what we understand, and this book points at its holes.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0111, 'book-hs', 16, 97, 'unmarked', "A break in the sequence would be a place where something showed up that the previous step couldn't supply — and in every transition that has been worked out in detail, nothing like that has been found.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0112, 'book-hs', 16, 99, 'unmarked', "That's a claim about the steps we understand.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0113, 'book-hs', 16, 99, 'unmarked', "It is not a promise about the one we don't.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0114, 'book-hs', 16, 101, 'unmarked', "Which is where the book ends, and where it said it would.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0115, 'book-hs', 16, 101, 'unmarked', "The questions it leaves open are left open on the page, with the arguments still standing next to each other, because that's more useful to you than a tidy ending would be.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0116, 'book-hs', 16, 103, 'unmarked', "The way to tell a real pattern from a convincing one is to go and check.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0117, 'book-hs', 16, 109, 'unmarked', "Everything in this book came from somewhere, and most of those somewheres are more interesting than the summary.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0118, 'book-hs', 16, 111, 'unmarked', "If the chemistry grabbed you, look up the formose reaction, Bénard cells, and the Belousov–Zhabotinsky reaction — the last one you can watch on video, and you should.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0119, 'book-hs', 16, 113, 'unmarked', "If the bags did, search for protocells and fatty acid vesicles.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0120, 'book-hs', 16, 115, 'unmarked', "If evolution's leftovers did, look up the recurrent laryngeal nerve and the evolution of mammalian ear bones, which is one of the best-documented transitions in all of palaeontology.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0121, 'book-hs', 16, 117, 'unmarked', "If the spirals did, look up phyllotaxis and the Douady and Couder droplet experiment.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0122, 'book-hs', 16, 119, 'unmarked', "If brains did, read Hofstadter's Gödel, Escher, Bach — it's long, it's strange, and it's worth it.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0123, 'book-hs', 16, 121, 'unmarked', "If the corn did, look up nixtamalization and pellagra, and notice how recently this was all worked out.").
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0124, 'book-hs', 16, 123, 'unmarked', "And if you want to know how reliable any particular claim in this book is: chapter 17, at the back, names the sources and marks the ones whose support hasn't been fully checked yet.").
xref(s_bookhs_16_0124, 17).
sentence(s_bookhs_16_0125, 'book-hs', 16, 123, 'unmarked', "The longer edition also says which chapter leans on each one.").
chapter('book-hs', 17, "17-where-this-comes-from.md", "17. Where this comes from").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0001, 'book-hs', 17, 3, 'unmarked', "These are the sources behind this book.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0002, 'book-hs', 17, 3, 'unmarked', "It's the same list the longer edition uses, because both editions rest on the same research.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0003, 'book-hs', 17, 3, 'unmarked', "The longer edition also says which of its chapters lean on each source.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0004, 'book-hs', 17, 5, 'unmarked', "Every entry was checked against the publication record for its authors, year, title and other details.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0005, 'book-hs', 17, 5, 'unmarked', "Whether each source really supports the sentence that leans on it is a harder question.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0006, 'book-hs', 17, 5, 'unmarked', "Most were checked against the source's own summary, and the most important claims much more deeply.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0007, 'book-hs', 17, 5, 'unmarked', "A † means the sentence hasn't yet been checked against the source itself, not even its summary.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0008, 'book-hs', 17, 5, 'unmarked', "Treat it as a pointer to where to look, not as proof that the looking is done.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0009, 'book-hs', 17, 7, 'unmarked', "Most entries end with a web address starting with https://doi.org/.").
sentence(s_bookhs_17_0010, 'book-hs', 17, 7, 'unmarked', "That's a permanent link to the work.").
